   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r3": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "84. The virtue of courage of a heroic person cannot",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "be obliterated though he be worried; though pointed down-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "wards, the flame of fire does not point to the ground.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r4": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "85. That courageous man conquers the triple world",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "whose mind the arrow-like side-glances of women do not",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "hurt, the heat-of-fire-like anger does not burn and the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "numerous sensual objects do not draw ( towards them ) with",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "their captivating snares.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r5": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "87. Better if this body falls from the lofty peak of a",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "high mountain against some rugged surface and is shattered",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "to pieces in the midst of rough rocks; better is the hand",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "thrust into the fangs of a huge serpent of deadly bite;",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "better falling into the fire; but not the wrecking of one's",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "character.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r6": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "88. The fire acts like water, the ocean becomes like {a",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "streamlet, Meru like a small stone, the lion like a deer, the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "serpent like a wreath of flowers, and poisonous juice like a",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "shower of nectar, to him in whose person becomes manifest",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "good character which is prized most} by all men.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r7": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "94. When I see the sun and the moon oppressed by the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "planet ( Râhu ), the captivity of the elephant and the snake",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "and the poverty of men of intellect, I come to think—Oh,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "destiny is all powerful !",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r8": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "95. In the first place, the Creator creates an excellent",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "man, the ornament of the earth and the mine of all good",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "qualities; but if he makes him short-lived, then alas ! woe to",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "the indiscretion of Vidhi !",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r9": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "96. Though he is the repository of nectar, and the lord",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "of herbs, though he is followed by S'atabhishak ( the con-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "",
     "end": "join"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
